cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "CP-DFIR: Cross-Platform DFIR Framework"
version: "1.3"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Vasava
    given-names: Jayveer
    affiliation: "Parul University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jayveerv/DFIR-Framework-WebApp"
url: "https://cp-dfir-console.onrender.com/"
abstract: >-
  CP-DFIR collects evidence from Windows, Linux and AWS, converts it to one
  common schema, and correlates events from the different platforms into a
  single attack timeline mapped to MITRE ATT&CK. Every step is recorded in a
  tamper-evident, HMAC-signed chain-of-custody ledger, and every finding can be
  exported as a Merkle per-finding proof that is checked against the ledger
  root. It runs as a browser-based analyst console and from the command line.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
  - DFIR
  - cross-platform correlation
  - cloud forensics
  - AWS CloudTrail
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - chain of custody
  - Merkle tree
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23973650
date-released: "2026-11-05"
